Subject: [PATCH] Remove Fermata Mirror launcher entry, donate menu, and GitHub update check

Fork-behavior changes for a self-distributed sideload build. Three independent edits:

1) Remove "Fermata Mirror" from the Android Auto launcher
   Comment out the MirrorService <service> registration in the auto manifest. Only the
   manifest registration is removed; MirrorService.java and the shared
   MirrorActivity/MirrorDisplay classes are left intact (still used by MirrorServiceFS and
   LauncherActivity). CarService keeps its own CATEGORY_PROJECTION filter, so the primary
   Android Auto media entry is unaffected.

2) Remove the "Coffee for developer" (donate) nav-menu option
   Comment out the donate item in NavBarMediator.showMenu() (R.id.nav_donate). The handler
   block is left in place but is now unreachable.

3) Disable the startup GitHub update check
   checkUpdates() now returns immediately (whole method is a no-op). The original logic
   queried api.github.com/repos/AndreyPavlenko/Fermata/releases/latest and, for a fork,
   would prompt users toward the upstream APK. The DELETE_ON_STARTUP cleanup it contained
   only ever serviced the updater, so it is correctly skipped too. The "Check for updates
   on startup" Settings row is removed from SettingsFragment.

APPLY ORDER: apply after 0001 + 0002 + play-publishable-disable-carappservice.patch
(the auto-manifest hunk below assumes the publishability patch is already applied, since
both edit fermata/src/auto/AndroidManifest.xml).
---
diff --git a/fermata/src/auto/AndroidManifest.xml b/fermata/src/auto/AndroidManifest.xml
index 1ab7e90..958844c 100644
--- a/fermata/src/auto/AndroidManifest.xml
+++ b/fermata/src/auto/AndroidManifest.xml
@@ -59,7 +65,12 @@
             </intent-filter>
         </service>
 
-        <service
+        <!-- "Fermata Mirror" (phone-screen mirroring) entry removed from the Android Auto launcher.
+             Only the manifest registration is commented out; MirrorService.java and the shared
+             MirrorActivity/MirrorDisplay classes are left intact (still used by MirrorServiceFS and
+             LauncherActivity). CarService keeps its own CATEGORY_PROJECTION filter, so the primary
+             Android Auto media entry is unaffected. -->
+        <!--<service
             android:name="me.aap.fermata.auto.MirrorService"
             android:exported="true"
             android:icon="@drawable/mirror"
@@ -71,7 +82,7 @@
                 <category android:name="com.google.android.gms.car.category.CATEGORY_PROJECTION" />
                 <category android:name="com.google.android.gms.car.category.CATEGORY_PROJECTION_OEM" />
             </intent-filter>
-        </service>
+        </service>-->
 
         <service
             android:name="me.aap.fermata.auto.MirrorServiceFS"
